  :definition-cid
  {:status :implemented
   :implementation "src/kotoba/lang/code_identity.cljc"
   :payload-version 2
   :canonical-input [:typed-kir :profile-version :desugar-contract-version
                     :effect-row :interface :direct-definition-dependencies]
   :excludes [:source-formatting :package-name :git-ref :wasm-compiler-incidental-output]
   ;; Widened from :closed-deterministic-pure-definition on 2026-09-02 (owner
   ;; decision, Unison-style deepening). The mechanism already sealed the effect
   ;; row at payload version 2 and the frozen vectors already carried effectful
   ;; rows; lang/typed-eval.edn already evaluates effectful definitions by CID.
   ;; Only this word said "pure", and it contradicted all three.
   :scope :closed-deterministic-checked-definition
   :effectful {:status :sealed-by-effect-row
               :evidence "lang/code-identity-vectors.edn :effect-row-http / :effect-row-two"
               :conformance ["lang/code-identity-conformance/positive/identity_effectful_http.edn"
                             "lang/code-identity-conformance/positive/locked_effectful_definition_admitted.edn"]
               :note "An effectful definition has a CID and it differs from the same KIR with an empty row. The CID is identity, never authority: evaluating it still requires the receipt lang/typed-eval.edn names."}
   ;; Measured 2026-09-02 against kotoba-sema frontend.cljc (direct-facts,
   ;; normalize-effect-ceiling) and kotoba-kir definition-identity
   ;; (effect-row-problem): the compiler's inferred rows carry [:cap/call id]
   ;; wire vectors; the identity admits keyword members only. Bridged the same
   ;; day: the sealed row is the SEMANTIC row -- named operations as keywords
   ;; -- because the numeric id is wire ABI (see :ability :source-model below:
   ;; "numeric IDs and portable envelopes are elaboration targets", and
   ;; lang/capability-catalog.edn :numeric-id :not-user-facing). A catalog
   ;; renumbering must not move a definition's identity.
   :effect-row-vocabulary
   {:accepted :keyword-members
    :sealed :named-operations-as-keywords
    :compiler-produces "[:cap/call id] vectors, plus :named-operations (the keywords ability elaboration recorded)"
    :status :bridged
    :adapter "kotoba.kir.definition-identity/effect-row-from-hir"
    :adapter-input "{:effects #{[:cap/call 8] ...} :named-operations #{:state/transact ...}} + {:id->name kotoba.sema/capability-id->name}"
    :adapter-note "kotoba-sema owns the catalog and depends on kotoba-kir, so the id->name mapping is an argument to the bridge, never a lookup the identity makes. The bridge adds no encoding: a bridged row hashes to exactly the bytes a hand-resolved keyword row hashes to."
    :refusal "definition effect row members must be keywords"
    :unnamed-wire-id-refusal "effect row wire id has no catalog name: [:cap/call 200]"
    :refusals ["a wire id the catalog cannot name (never guessed; ex-data :problem :definition/effect-row-unbridged)"
               "a member that is not [:cap/call <integer>] (the compiler never emits one, so it is not a compiler row)"
               "a catalog mapping two wire ids to one name (would seal two wire rows as one identity)"
               "a :named-operations member the catalog does not know (closed world, as the compiler's cap-call keyword)"]
    :evidence ["kotoba-lang/kotoba-kir test/kotoba/kir_definition_identity_test.clj compiler-wire-effect-rows-are-refused-and-bridged / unnamed-wire-ids-are-refused-not-guessed / every-frozen-vector-is-byte-identical-after-the-bridge"
               "lang/code-identity-conformance/positive/identity_named_operation_row.edn (row produced by the bridge)"
               "scripts/verify_code_identity_cljs.cljs (BigInt ids under nbb bridge to the same row; the unnamed-id refusal is the same literal)"]
    :note "The identity itself still refuses a wire row -- that refusal is what keeps the ABI out of the sealed bytes. Effectful DefCIDs are minted from the keyword row the bridge returns. All 10 frozen vectors are byte-identical before and after the bridge (asserted in both repositories)."}
   :codec :dag-cbor
   :multihash :sha2-256
   :note "Identity is computed after desugar, type/effect checking, and ability elaboration."
   ;; Payload version 1 sealed only profile-version, typed-kir, interface and
   ;; dependencies, and addressed pr-str output under a dag-cbor label. Both
   ;; were defects: a pure definition and an effectful one with identical KIR
   ;; shared a CID, and pr-str is not byte-identical across implementations.
   :supersedes {:payload-version 1
                :reason [:effect-row-unsealed :desugar-contract-version-unsealed
                         :codec-mislabelled :not-cross-implementation-deterministic]}
   :exact-value-forms
   {:reason "A ClojureScript reader rounds integer literals past 2^53-1 and has one number type, so some values are corrupted before any encoder sees them."
    :i64 "kotoba.lang.code-identity/i64 — exact decimal text; plain integers admitted within ±(2^53-1)"
    :f64 "kotoba.lang.code-identity/f64 — exact IEEE-754 bits as 16 hex characters; raw platform floats are refused"}}
