 ;; Measured 2026-09-02: two algorithms answer "what is this definition".
 ;; ADR-2608550000 (superproject, accepted 2026-08-04) named exactly this --
 ;; two answers to one question -- as the defect it was fixing, and converged
 ;; L0 identity on the compiler's checked KIR through kotoba.codebase.typed-code.
 ;; That namespace does not call kotoba.kir.definition-identity (the
 ;; implementation this contract names under :identities :definition-cid); it
 ;; hashes its own canonical form with different bytes.
 :identity-implementations
 {:authority :kotoba.kir/definition-identity
  :kotoba.kir/definition-identity
  {:status :authority
   :repo "kotoba-lang/kotoba-kir"
   :namespace "kotoba.kir.definition-identity"
   :payload-version 2
   :canonical-input [:typed-kir :profile-version :desugar-contract-version
                     :effect-row :interface :direct-definition-dependencies]
   :encoding "one canonical DAG-CBOR block; interface and effect row inline; effect row = named operations as keywords"
   :cross-implementation "JVM and ClojureScript byte-identical on all 10 frozen vectors (CI6)"
   :facade "src/kotoba/lang/code_identity.cljc (this repository) delegates every function to it"}
  :kotoba.codebase/typed-code
  {:status :second-implementation-to-be-migrated
   :repo "kotoba-lang/codebase"
   :namespace "kotoba.codebase.typed-code"
   :schema "kotoba.typed-definition.v1 (contract-version 1; group members kotoba.typed-group.v1 / kotoba.typed-member.v1)"
   :calls-definition-identity false
   :encoding "own canonical-form + own alpha-normalization; interface is a separate block (kotoba.typed-interface.v1) linked by CID; profile and hash-contract as CID links; effects encoded as (vec (sort (map stable-name effects))) -- stable-name falls through to str, so a compiler wire row [:cap/call 9] is sealed as the string \"[:cap/call 9]\" rather than refused or translated"
   :consumers ["kotoba-lang/codebase typed_eval.cljc / render.clj / authoring.clj"
               "kotoba-lang/kotoba src/kotoba/codebase_typed.clj, launcher.clj (kotoba codebase add --typed), library_release.clj, reference_package.clj"]}
  :measured-difference
  {:date "2026-09-02"
   :method "kotoba-lang/codebase test/kotoba/codebase/typed_code_identity_divergence_test.clj: one function presented to both algorithms"
   :cases [{:definition "(defn double [x] (* x 2)), pure"
            :typed-code "bafyreihetwjs6fjj63z5zqnho7befbvw2h5igtmvujuaaiqfnjrg5uq7yq"
            :definition-identity "bafyreigk5ahn6xqt4hxtpwbzxnwd6wvzsljpcwfwm57c2tapqqxlbw75pa"}
           {:definition "(defn emit [x] (typed-cap-call 9 :i64 :i64 x)), compiler row #{[:cap/call 9]}"
            :typed-code "bafyreibsdyuxvctmdtocmrwidacdflmq7disy7h2oogvsf4u2hyye75gcq"
            :definition-identity "bafyreifwxv5eyc3qcvoidimcbw6usngoiccmdrucvrtwi7gs5vef5ugymy (effect row bridged to #{:log/write})"}]
   :effect-row "typed-code: [\"[:cap/call 9]\"] (string of the wire vector; typed-eval reads it back with (map keyword)). definition-identity: refuses the wire row; seals #{:log/write} via effect-row-from-hir."
   :persistence "No typed-code CID is committed in any fixture, README or resource of kotoba-lang/codebase (40b3d53), kotoba-lang/kotoba (eca2bead5) or kotoba-lang/kotobase (1df165d) (git grep for the schema strings and the namespace, 2026-09-02). Local codebase stores (kotoba codebase add --typed, library_release/build!) and kotobase.storage providers (backend/kotobase.clj) are not enumerable from here: whether any typed-code CID is persisted there is UNVERIFIED."}
  :direction
  {:decision :typed-code-adopts-definition-identity
   :statement "kotoba.codebase.typed-code adopts kotoba.kir.definition-identity as its hashing core, with a versioned migration: a new typed-definition schema/contract-version whose definition CID IS the payload-v2 DefCID, and whose effect row is the named-operation row from effect-row-from-hir. The old schema stays readable; nothing is rewritten in place."
   :migration-cost "Every stored typed-code CID moves (identity, interface, group and member blocks). Committed cost measured 2026-09-02: zero persisted CIDs found in the repositories above. Unmeasured cost: user-local stores and kotobase providers (UNVERIFIED above) -- which is why the migration is versioned rather than an in-place re-encoding, and why it is not part of the change that recorded this entry."
   :until-then "kotoba-lang/codebase pins the divergence: typed_code_identity_divergence_test.clj asserts the two CIDs DIFFER and that typed-code seals the wire row as a string, so neither side can be changed to agree silently. When the migration lands that test becomes an equality test on purpose."}}

